{"type": "step", "node_id": 23, "parent_node_id": 22, "role": "assistant", "content": "## Solution\n\n**Setup.** Let $S = t_1+t_2+t_3+t_4$ and $T = t_5+t_6+t_7$, so $S+T = 270$. The constraints are $S \\equiv 0 \\pmod 7$ and $T \\equiv 0 \\pmod{13}$, i.e. $S \\equiv 270 \\pmod{13}$.\n\n**Finding valid $S$.** We compute $270 \\bmod 7 = 4$ and $270 \\bmod{13} = 10$. So we need\n$$S \\equiv 0 \\pmod 7, \\qquad S \\equiv 10 \\pmod{13}.$$\nSince $\\gcd(7,13)=1$, by CRT the solution is unique mod $91$. Writing $S=7k$: $7k\\equiv 10\\pmod{13}$, and $7^{-1}\\equiv 2\\pmod{13}$, so $k\\equiv 20\\equiv 7\\pmod{13}$, giving $S = 7(13m+7)=91m+49$, i.e. $S\\equiv 49\\pmod{91}$.\n\nWith $0\\le S\\le 270$, the valid values are $S\\in\\{49,\\,140,\\,231\\}$.\n\n**Counting scenarios for each $S$.** For a fixed $S$, the number of non-negative integer solutions to $t_1+t_2+t_3+t_4=S$ is $\\binom{S+3}{3}$, and to $t_5+t_6+t_7 = 270-S$ is $\\binom{272-S}{2}$. The total count is\n$$\\sum_{S\\in\\{49,140,231\\}} \\binom{S+3}{3}\\binom{272-S}{2}.$$\n\n**Evaluating each term:**\n\n- $S=49$: $\\binom{52}{3}\\binom{223}{2} = 22100 \\times 24753 = 547{,}041{,}300.$\n- $S=140$: $\\binom{143}{3}\\binom{132}{2} = 477{,}191 \\times 8{,}646 = 4{,}125{,}793{,}386.$\n- $S=231$: $\\binom{234}{3}\\binom{41}{2} = 2{,}108{,}184 \\times 820 = 1{,}728{,}710{,}880.$\n\n**Summing:**\n$$547{,}041{,}300 + 4{,}125{,}793{,}386 + 1{,}728{,}710{,}880 = 6{,}401{,}545{,}566.$$\n\nThe number of different scenarios is $\\boxed{6{,}401{,}545{,}566}$.\n\n### PROOF COMPLETE", "thinking": "Let me solve this problem. We have 7 technicians, total 270 minutes distributed as non-negative integers (t1,...,t7) summing to 270. Constraints: t1+t2+t3+t4 ≡ 0 mod 7, and t5+t6+t7 ≡ 0 mod 13.\n\nLet S = t1+t2+t3+t4, T = t5+t6+t7. S+T = 270. S ≡ 0 mod 7, T ≡ 0 mod 13.\n\n270 mod 7 = 270 - 252 = 18, 18 mod 7 = 4. So 270 ≡ 4 mod 7.\n270 mod 13 = 270 - 260 = 10. So 270 ≡ 10 mod 13.\n\nWe need S ≡ 0 mod 7 and T = 270 - S ≡ 0 mod 13, i.e., S ≡ 270 ≡ 10 mod 13.\n\nSo S ≡ 0 mod 7 and S ≡ 10 mod 13. CRT: 7 and 13 coprime. S ≡ ? mod 91.\n\nS ≡ 0 mod 7: S = 7k. 7k ≡ 10 mod 13. 7k ≡ 10 mod 13. 7^{-1} mod 13: 7*2=14≡1, so 7^{-1}=2. k ≡ 20 ≡ 7 mod 13. So k = 13m+7, S = 7(13m+7) = 91m + 49. So S ≡ 49 mod 91.\n\nS ranges 0 to 270. S = 49, 140, 231. (49+91=140, 140+91=231, 231+91=322>270). So three possible S values: 49, 140, 231.\n\nFor each S, number of ways to distribute S among 4 people = C(S+3,3), and distribute T=270-S among 3 people = C(T+2,2) = C(270-S+2,2) = C(272-S,2).\n\nTotal = Σ over S∈{49,140,231} of C(S+3,3)·C(272-S,2).\n\nS=49: C(52,3)·C(223,2) = (52·51·50/6)·(223·222/2) = 22100 · 24753.\n52*51*50/6 = 52*51*50 = 132600, /6 = 22100. ✓\n223*222/2 = 223*111 = 24753. ✓\n22100 * 24753 = ?\n\nS=140: C(143,3)·C(132,2) = (143·142·141/6)·(132·131/2).\n143*142*141 = 143*142 = 20306, *141 = 20306*141 = 20306*140 + 20306 = 2842840 + 20306 = 2863146. /6 = 477191.\n132*131/2 = 66*131 = 8646.\n477191 * 8646 = ?\n\nS=231: C(234,3)·C(41,2) = (234·233·232/6)·(41·40/2).\n234*233*232 = 234*233 = 54522, *232 = 54522*232 = 54522*200 + 54522*32 = 10904400 + 1744704 = 12649104. /6 = 2108184.\n41*40/2 = 820.\n2108184 * 820 = ?\n\nLet me compute each.\n\n22100 * 24753:\n22100 * 24753 = 22100 * 24000 + 22100*753 = 530400000 + 22100*753.\n22100*753 = 22100*700 + 22100*53 = 15470000 + 1171300 = 16641300.\nTotal = 530400000 + 16641300 = 547041300.\n\n477191 * 8646:\n477191 * 8646 = 477191*8000 + 477191*646.\n477191*8000 = 3817528000.\n477191*646 = 477191*600 + 477191*46 = 286314600 + 477191*46.\n477191*46 = 477191*40 + 477191*6 = 19087640 + 2863146 = 21950786.\n477191*646 = 286314600 + 21950786 = 308265386.\nTotal = 3817528000 + 308265386 = 4125793386.\n\n2108184 * 820:\n2108184 * 820 = 2108184*800 + 2108184*20 = 1686547200 + 42163680 = 1728710880.\n\nSum = 547041300 + 4125793386 + 1728710880.\n547041300 + 4125793386 = 4672834686.\n4672834686 + 1728710880 = 6401545566.\n\nLet me double-check the arithmetic.\n\n547041300 + 4125793386:\n547041300 + 4125793386 = 4672834686. ✓\n\n4672834686 + 1728710880 = 6401545566. ✓\n\nLet me verify each product again.\n\n22100 × 24753:\n24753 × 22100 = 24753 × 221 × 100.\n24753 × 221 = 24753×200 + 24753×21 = 4950600 + 519813 = 5470413.\n× 100 = 547041300. ✓\n\n477191 × 8646:\nLet me redo. 477191 × 8646.\n477191 × 8000 = 3,817,528,000.\n477191 × 600 = 286,314,600.\n477191 × 40 = 19,087,640.\n477191 × 6 = 2,863,146.\nSum: 3,817,528,000 + 286,314,600 = 4,103,842,600.\n+ 19,087,640 = 4,122,930,240.\n+ 2,863,146 = 4,125,793,386. ✓\n\n2108184 × 820:\n2,108,184 × 800 = 1,686,547,200.\n2,108,184 × 20 = 42,163,680.\nSum = 1,728,710,880. ✓\n\nTotal: 547,041,300 + 4,125,793,386 + 1,728,710,880.\n547,041,300 + 4,125,793,386 = 4,672,834,686.\n4,672,834,686 + 1,728,710,880 = 6,401,545,566. ✓\n\nSo the answer is 6,401,545,566.\n\nLet me verify the stars and bars counts. Number of non-negative integer solutions to t1+t2+t3+t4 = S is C(S+4-1, 4-1) = C(S+3,3). ✓. Number for t5+t6+t7 = T is C(T+2,2). ✓.\n\nNow verify S values. S ≡ 0 mod 7, S ≡ 10 mod 13. CRT gives S ≡ 49 mod 91. Check: 49 mod 7 = 0 ✓. 49 mod 13 = 49-39=10 ✓. S in [0,270]: 49, 140, 231. 231+91=322>270 ✓. 49-91<0 ✓.\n\nC(52,3): 52*51*50/6 = 132600/6 = 22100 ✓.\nC(223,2): 223*222/2 = 49506/2 = 24753 ✓.\nC(143,3): 143*142*141/6. 143*142=20306, *141=2863146, /6=477191 ✓.\nC(132,2): 132*131/2 = 17292/2 = 8646 ✓.\nC(234,3): 234*233*232/6. 234*233=54522, *232=12649104, /6=2108184 ✓.\nC(41,2): 41*40/2=820 ✓.\n\nAll checks pass. Answer: 6,401,545,566.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786759225}
